From 2629e279cd7d0284c4b40be1ff8ebfee111625a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:12:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] analysis: null integrity (EIA0) detector

Adds the `null_integrity` analyzer: flags a NAS Security Mode Command that
selects the null integrity algorithm EIA0 (High).

EIA0 leaves NAS signalling with no integrity protection, so the network cannot be
authenticated and signalling can be forged -- a harder false-base-station
indicator than null ciphering (EEA0), which the companion `nas_null_cipher`
analyzer already covers via the ciphering algorithm. 3GPP permits EIA0 only for an
unauthenticated emergency-services attach (TS 33.401 5.1.4.1), so a genuine
emergency call is the main benign trigger; off by default pending calibration.

Stateless; reads `EMMSecurityModeCommand.nas_sec_algo.integ_algo`, the integrity
counterpart of the field nas_null_cipher reads.

Test harness: uses `analysis::test_util::emm_message` with a Security Mode Command
body adapted from the pycrate test vector; tests cover EIA0 (High), a real
algorithm (not flagged), a non-SMC EMM message, and a non-LTE IE, plus
AnalyzerConfig default-off and Harness wiring in analyzer.rs.

Ref: Orbic-Rayhunter T-OR-055; ref-docs/lte-imsi-catcher-detection.md 3.6.
Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
